## 4. Kill-switch identity

GEN_TABLE_3

The identity holds in all 12 class rows. So the two arms of every cell scored the same positions, and the kernel dispatch is the only controlled difference between the arms (the kill switch flips only available(); same layout, same AVX dotter). A cross-arm time or TPS difference is therefore the kernel effect plus single-repetition variation. The rows where the kernel ran in neither arm (gpt-oss, qwen under FPGA attention) bound that variation at about 1 to 2 % of T1, TPS and TTFT and up to 5 % of busy per job; only differences above that are attributed to the kernel.

